{"id": 32, "ts": 1780467443.4649804, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I concur with Sarah\u2019s shift to Candidate\u202fC as the provisional front\u2011runner.\u202fC\u2019s record shows 100\u202f% reliability, the ability to make correct decisions quickly, excellent attention skills, and a calm demeanor in crises\u2014core safety criteria for long\u2011distance operations. Moreover, he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d directly addressing crew\u2011cooperation, which we lack for B and A. While C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and his egocentric reputation raise concerns about professional communication and adaptability, these issues are less severe than B\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks about his colleagues,\u201d which constitute a clear breach of professional communication and likely undermine crew dynamics. Compared with Candidate\u202fA, we have no evidence of A\u2019s stress\u2011resilience or decision quality under pressure, and Candidate\u202fD remains largely unevaluated. Therefore, based on the evidence presently available, Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit."}
